    "text": "Let G be a finitely generated group, and N a minimal normal subgroup of G\nwhich is an elementary abelian p-group. Is it true that either N is finite or the growth\nfunction for the elements of N with respect to a finite generating set of G is bounded\nbelow by an exponential function?                                          V. I. Trofimov",
